### Tier 2 marketplace demo — REST Client requests
### Open in VS Code with the REST Client extension and run requests top-to-bottom.
### Seed product IDs are dynamic at Tier 2 (no deterministic Guids); the chained
### named requests below fetch them at runtime.

@host = http://localhost:5000
@sellerId = 11111111-1111-1111-1111-111111111111
@buyerId  = 22222222-2222-2222-2222-222222222222
@otherBuyerId = 44444444-4444-4444-4444-444444444444
@adminId  = 33333333-3333-3333-3333-333333333333

### Fetch published products (alphabetical: Doohickey, Gizmo, Widget)
# @name listed
GET {{host}}/api/buyer/products
X-User-Role: Buyer
X-User-Id: {{buyerId}}

### S1: Seller creates a product -> 201
POST {{host}}/api/seller/products
X-User-Role: Seller
X-User-Id: {{sellerId}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "name": "Sample Widget", "price": 15.00, "stock": 25 }

### S2: Create product with empty name -> 400
POST {{host}}/api/seller/products
X-User-Role: Seller
X-User-Id: {{sellerId}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "name": "", "price": 10.00, "stock": 5 }

### S3: Create product with price = 0 -> 400
POST {{host}}/api/seller/products
X-User-Role: Seller
X-User-Id: {{sellerId}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "name": "Free Sample", "price": 0, "stock": 5 }

### S4: Buyer places an order with sufficient stock (Widget) -> 201, Confirmed
# @name placeOrder
POST {{host}}/api/buyer/orders
X-User-Role: Buyer
X-User-Id: {{buyerId}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "productId": "{{listed.response.body.$[2].id}}", "quantity": 2 }

### S5: Buyer places an order with insufficient stock (Doohickey stock=0) -> 422
POST {{host}}/api/buyer/orders
X-User-Role: Buyer
X-User-Id: {{buyerId}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "productId": "{{listed.response.body.$[0].id}}", "quantity": 1 }

### S7: Buyer cancels their own order -> 200
POST {{host}}/api/buyer/orders/{{placeOrder.response.body.$.orderId}}/cancel
X-User-Role: Buyer
X-User-Id: {{buyerId}}

### S8: Another buyer tries to cancel the same order (it's already cancelled, but with a different buyer first to demo NotOwner)
# Place another order so we can demo S8 against an active order:
# @name secondOrder
POST {{host}}/api/buyer/orders
X-User-Role: Buyer
X-User-Id: {{buyerId}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "productId": "{{listed.response.body.$[1].id}}", "quantity": 1 }

### Other buyer attempting to cancel buyer's order -> 403
POST {{host}}/api/buyer/orders/{{secondOrder.response.body.$.orderId}}/cancel
X-User-Role: Buyer
X-User-Id: {{otherBuyerId}}

### S9: Admin force-cancels an order -> 200
POST {{host}}/api/admin/orders/{{secondOrder.response.body.$.orderId}}/cancel
X-User-Role: Admin
X-User-Id: {{adminId}}

### S10: Buyer lists published products (suspended hidden)
GET {{host}}/api/buyer/products
X-User-Role: Buyer
X-User-Id: {{buyerId}}

### S11: Admin lists ALL products (including suspended)
GET {{host}}/api/admin/products
X-User-Role: Admin
X-User-Id: {{adminId}}

### S12: No role headers -> 401
GET {{host}}/api/buyer/products

### S13: Wrong role for endpoint -> 403
POST {{host}}/api/seller/products
X-User-Role: Buyer
X-User-Id: {{buyerId}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "name": "Naughty", "price": 1.00, "stock": 1 }
